   "category": "procedural",
   "complexity": "intermediate",
   "description": "The procedural-generation seam. An open world promises infinite variety; the truth is a finite formula fed one number. Nothing is stored - not the mountains, not the coastline - only the seed and the recipe. Walk away and the terrain is freed from memory; walk back and it rebuilds bit-for-bit from the same seed. Two visits to one seed, drawn identical, because they are not two worlds but one number run twice.",
